From f98b064ab7d1df08a13bc4de81c6f10196d609eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 05:27:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: onboard team members from the moment they're added, not
 their first task
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the actual gap behind "how do they know what this is" — a team member
with no open task who messaged the bot was treated as a customer (fell
through the hard task-gate in handleTeamMemberMessage entirely). Adding
someone to /agent/team also sent them nothing until they were first assigned
work.

- delegation.js: handleTasklessMemberMessage recognizes a member from add,
  not first task — /help and /mytasks handled deterministically (no LLM call,
  since this only decides routing), a plain greeting gets the same explainer,
  and anything customer-shaped still falls through unchanged (reuses the
  exact signal regex already proven in replyEngine.js's supplier-quote path).
  sendMemberWelcome DMs the moment a member is added via sendAsOwnerOrBot,
  never fails the add if Telegram rejects it (member hasn't opened the bot
  yet), and surfaces that hint back to the dashboard instead of the owner
  only discovering it via a manual Test DM. registerMemberCommands scopes
  /help and /mytasks to that member's chat only, mirroring the owner's
  existing per-chat setMyCommands pattern from the bot-link flow.
- delegationLogic.mjs: classifyTasklessMemberText, pure and unit-tested.
- teamBrain.js: registers the same command menu on first contact as a
  safety net for members added before this shipped.
- replyEngine.js: dtask_help_mytasks button (task-independent, same pattern
  as the existing dtask_groupoff special case).
- taskRunner.js: the client brief-back on task completion now grounds itself
  in the business name and what it's about, for a client who may not
  remember the conversation days later.
- agent/team/route.js + page.js: welcome-on-add wiring, and a collapsed-by-
  default "How delegation works" section on the team page explaining
  assignment/trust levels/team group in the app's own style (not the
  unrelated pre-signup HowItWorks carousel, which turned out to be hardcoded
  to a different topic and not designed to take custom content).

5 new unit tests (82/82 full suite); npx next build clean.

